# Fragtrack db backup — environment variable reference
#
# Copy the matching example into an ignored local file:
#   cp .env.example .env.development.local
#   cp .env.example .env.production.local
#
# NEVER commit .env.*.local. These files contain credentials.
# Process environment values fill variables absent from these files. If a
# variable exists in both with DIFFERENT values, the loader fails with a
# CONFLICT <VARIABLE> error naming it (values are never reported).
#
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID is the exception: the dotenv file value always wins,
# so a global shell export cannot redirect the R2 endpoint. A present file
# that omits it FAILS (the export is not used) — see the precedence note
# above. Only when no dotenv file exists at all (CI) may the process export
# configure the run.

# Which environment this file belongs to. Must be 'development' or 'production'
# and must match the selected --environment flag.
# BACKUP_ENVIRONMENT=development
#
# `vp run backup:local --environment …` consumes only BACKUP_ENVIRONMENT,
# SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF, and PROJECT_WORKDIR. Hosted DB, R2, age, and private
# identity fields are not resolved, validated, or returned for local backups.
# The selected environment labels the package and selects the target project
# ref; the data source stays the local Fragtrack stack. Row data is stored
# in PLAINTEXT gzip parts (no encryption). `vp run restore:development|
# restore:production --source local …` needs neither ENCRYPT_KEY (hosted-only)
# nor DECRYPT_KEY for plaintext snapshots (a legacy encrypted local snapshot
# still requires DECRYPT_KEY + age).

# Supabase project reference (20 lowercase alphanumeric characters).
# SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF=

# Supabase session-pooler connection string, e.g.
#   postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres?sslmode=require
# or a matching direct URL:
#   postgres://postgres:<password>@db.<project-ref>.supabase.co:5432/postgres?sslmode=require
# Must use the postgresql:/postgres: scheme, SSL, and reference the project
# above. Never select a transaction-pooler URL for backup/restore.
# SUPABASE_DB_URL=
#
# Cloudflare account identifier (32 hexadecimal characters). The dotenv file
# value wins over any process-environment export (see precedence note above).
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=

# R2 bucket. MUST equal the selected environment exactly:
#   development -> development
#   production  -> production
# R2_BUCKET=development

# R2 S3 API credentials (Object Read & Write, scoped to the matching bucket).
# R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# Public age X25519 recipient for this environment (starts with 'age1...').
# ENCRYPT_KEY=

# Private age X25519 identity (AGE-SECRET-KEY-...). Required only by r2/repo
# restores (and legacy encrypted local snapshots). Never set this value when
# only backing up; `--source local` plaintext snapshots do not need it.
# DECRYPT_KEY=

# Path to the sibling Fragtrack project, resolved relative to this repository.
# Used by `vp run backup:local --environment …` (the local dump source) and
# `vp run restore:local --environment …`.
# PROJECT_WORKDIR=../fragtrack
